 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? That's usually a greased chain on a dry rear wheel. Spray some chain lube on the chain and let it run through for a few minutes. Don't use cooking oil, it turns gummy and makes it worse. A thin lube for winter is fine now, or wait until spring to clean and re lube. Spray the chain evenly, leaving the hanging end drier. Then use your chain tool to pull new links into place. Clean it with a mild soap and water and a microfibre brush. Yes, a good clean gets rid of the grime that carries the dust in.",
